# Rulebook, not bible

## Word choice

When talking about organized creative-writing reference material (world details, cast, species, politics, lore, misc notes), say **rulebook** — not **bible**.

**Do not use:** world bible, cast bible, story bible, series bible, or similar.

**OK:** rulebook, world rulebook, cast notes in the rulebook, “your rulebook entries,” etc.

## Not a project concept

**Rulebook** is **vocabulary only** — how Cursor should speak. It is **not**:

- A product or site name
- A LoreKeeper feature or branded UI label
- A formal concept name for Maestro’s, envDyst, Halalit, or other Odd Trove projects

Do not introduce “Rulebook” as a module, page title, or project unless the owner explicitly asks for that branding in the same conversation.
